   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Why? / The two maps"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "f sends the whole disk to the single point. g sends that point to the disk’s center."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "On X, the composition is the constant map 0. H(x,t) = (1−t)x deforms the identity to this constant map. On the one-point space Y, the other composition is already the identity."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The top and bottom Y pictures show exactly the same intermediate output. The homotopy is in X: at t = 0 it matches the original input above, and at t = 1 it matches the composition below. The homotopy need not be one-to-one."
  },
